<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kangxi Emperor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kangxi Emperor was one of the longest-reigning rulers in Chinese history, governing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> from 1661 to 1722. He suppressed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-three-feudatories">Revolt of the Three Feudatories</a> and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-family">Zheng family</a> in 1683. His reign completed the consolidation of Qing rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kangxi-emperor.jpg" alt="Kangxi Emperor" width="255" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author Qing Dynasty Court Painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B8%85%E5%9C%A3%E7%A5%96%E5%BA%B7%E7%86%99%E7%9A%87%E5%B8%9D%E6%9C%9D%E6%9C%8D%E5%83%8F.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
